          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You are in @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Mountain Stance]</p><hr /><p>You stomp, shaking the earth beneath you. Creatures on the ground within a @Template[emanation|distance:20] take damage equal to your Strength modifier (minimum 0), with a @Check[fortitude|against:class|basic] save against your class DC. On a failure, they also fall @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Prone]. After you use this action, you can't use it again for [[/r 1d4 #Recharge it]]{1d4 rounds}.</p><hr /><p><strong>Special</strong> If you have this feat, the Dexterity modifier cap to your AC while using Mountain Stance increases from +1 to +2.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 14
          },
          "prerequisites": {
